To take advantage of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>'s dual-display design, Apple is introducing new Camera app features that are unique to the foldable iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-cameras.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065340" /><br/>
<h2 id="smart_take">Smart Take</h2><br/>
Smart Take uses AI to determine when everyone (including the iPhone owner) is ready for a group shot, so no one has to use a timer or stay out of the picture to capture the image.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-camera-smart-take.jpg" alt="" width="1999" height="1123" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065341" /><br/>
You can prop up the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; in a half-folded orientation, get in frame, and then wait for the group shot to be taken.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="kid_cue">Kid Cue</h2><br/>
Kid Cue shows little Peanuts animations to children so they look at the camera when you're taking a photo.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-kid-cue.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1124" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065342" /><br/>
<h2 id="duo_preview">Duo Preview</h2><br/>
With Duo Preview, the Camera app shows a live preview of the shot on both displays, so the subject you're taking a photo of can make adjustments.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-preview-camera-app.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1124" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065343" /><br/>
<h2 id="duo_facetime">Duo FaceTime</h2><br/>
Nearby friends can participate in a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/facetime/">FaceTime</a> call using the outer display while the iPhone owner uses the inner display, so nobody has to crowd around the iPhone or pass it around to get on video.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-facetime.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063423" /><br/>
Duo &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; is not the same as Dual Capture, which records video with both the front and rear cameras. Duo &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; specifically uses the outer display to allow another person to join in on a call.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="unique_form_factor_features">Unique Form Factor Features</h2><br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; can be used in multiple orientations, including when it's half-folded. The Duo stands up on its own, for taking &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; calls and recording video without holding it.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-orientations.jpg" alt="" width="1901" height="1069" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065344" /><br/>
The folding mechanism acts like a built-in tripod and stand, so it's also useful for selfies and long exposures. You can also capture selfies with the higher-quality 48MP rear camera while using the outer display as a viewfinder, which isn't something you can do with a slab iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="camera_hardware">Camera Hardware</h2><br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; has a "Dual Fusion" two-camera setup with a 48MP Main camera. It's basically the same camera that's in the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a> (not the 17 Pro), offering 26mm 24MP images by default, along with 12MP 2x "telephoto" images at 52mm.<br/>
<br/>
The camera supports sensor-shift optical image stabilization, but not the second-generation version available in the Pro models. It also does not support spatial photos or the ProRAW format.<br/>
<br/>
It also includes a 48MP Ultra Wide camera with a 13mm focal length and macro capabilities. Since there's no Telephoto lens, the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is limited to 2x optical-quality zoom in, 2x optical zoom out, and digital zoom up to 10x for images.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="other_camera_capabilities">Other Camera Capabilities</h2><br/>
Like the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> and Pro Max, the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; supports the latest Photographic Styles, which adds texture and grain parameters.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="video">Video</h2><br/>
Smart focus tracking is a feature new to the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; and the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; models. It uses AI to keep a subject in focus at all times, and pick up subject tracking if the subject exits the frame and then reappears.<br/>
<br/>
The Duo supports 4K Dolby Vision video recording at up to 120 fps, and Cinematic mode for recording videos in 4K Dolby Vision at up to 60 fps. For the first time, Cinematic mode effects can be added to a video after capture on the Duo and &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj;. Apple also says there's improved low-light video on the Duo when recording at 1080p.<br/>
<br/>
Time-lapse video recording with stabilization up to 4K Dolby Vision is a new &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; and &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; option. It's especially useful on the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; because you can record a stable video without the need for a tripod.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="front_camera">Front Camera</h2><br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;'s outer front-facing camera is 12MP, not 18MP like the &zwnj;iPhone 17&zwnj; and &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; models. It otherwise has the same features.<br/>
<br/>
The inner display has a 1080p &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; camera that's under the display.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="missing_camera_features">Missing Camera Features</h2><br/>
Compared to the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; and Pro Max, the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; has a more rudimentary camera system. It lacks many features available on the Pro models.<br/>
<ul><br/>
 <li>Telephoto lens</li><br/>
 <li>Pro Controls</li><br/>
 <li>Apple Reference Image</li><br/>
 <li>Variable aperture</li><br/>
 <li>Second-generation sensor-shift optical image stabilization</li><br/>
 <li>Adaptive True Tone flash</li><br/>
 <li>Spatial photos and video recording</li><br/>
 <li>ProRAW</li><br/>
 <li>ProRes</li><br/>
 <li>ProRes RAW</li><br/>
 <li>Genlock</li><br/>
 <li>Apple Log 2 video recording</li><br/>
 <li>Studio-quality four-mic array</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
